# FX > SEL list > REV TYPE: a new project's reverb is CLASSIC (as every save from before the setting,
# whose slot is 0); a slot past the list's end (a damaged or newer save) reads as the engine plays
# it, ROOM; ROOM from the list; undo and redo carry it to the engine; undoing another edit leaves
# it; ROOM saved loads as ROOM
wait 300
expect sound4.1.1 0
expect rvtype 0
param 4 1 1 2
wait 50
expect rvtype 1
listen
tap FX
tap SEL
turn SELECT 7
wait 600
said REV TYPE ROOM
param 4 1 1 0
wait 50
expect rvtype 0
wait 600
shot revtype_list.png
turn ALGO 1
expect sound4.1.1 1
expect rvtype 1
shot revtype_room.png
# undo (HOME + REC): back to CLASSIC, in the engine too; redo (HOME + PLAY): ROOM again
wait 600
press HOME
tap REC
release HOME
wait 100
expect sound4.1.1 0
expect rvtype 0
press HOME
tap PLAY
release HOME
wait 100
expect sound4.1.1 1
expect rvtype 1
# another edit (DECAY), undone: the decay goes back, the type stays ROOM
wait 600
param 4 0 4 82
wait 600
press HOME
tap REC
release HOME
wait 100
expect sound4.0.4 73
expect sound4.1.1 1
expect rvtype 1
# saved with ROOM: loads with ROOM
tap HOME
tap SAVE
wait 300
reboot
wait 300
expect sound4.1.1 1
expect rvtype 1
